WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.540
2016 has been a long, brutal year for celebrity
deaths.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.040
In addition to the loss of renowned musicians
such as David Bowie and Prince, many screen

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.170
stars have also died this year, from cherished
character actors to major movie stars.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:18.710
Here's a look back at the actors and actresses
who passed away in 2016.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.009
Alan Rickman

00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:24.429
After joining the Royal Shakespeare Company
in England in the 1970s, Alan Rickman broke

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:29.929
out on the big screen in 1988, at the relatively
advanced age of 41 — but what a breakthrough

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.199
role it was.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:35.270
Playing the evil Hans Gruber in Die Hard set
in motion a career of playing some of Hollywood's

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:40.640
most iconic screen villains, such as the Sheriff
of Nottingham in Robin Hood: Prince of Thieves,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.490
Judge Turpin in Sweeney Todd, and the secret
good guy Professor Severus Snape in all eight

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:47.210
Harry Potter movies.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.970
Rickman died at age 69 after a battle with
pancreatic cancer.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:52.970
Gene Wilder

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.720
Few would disagree that Gene Wilder was a
comic genius.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.630
His collaborations with director Mel Brooks
were especially fruitful, spawning his memorable

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.290
turns in The Producers, Blazing Saddles, and
Young Frankenstein.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.770
"That's Frankenstein."

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:11.610
That would be enough of a legacy for any actor,
but Wilder also played the title role in Willy

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.890
Wonka and the Chocolate Factory and starred
in three buddy comedy movies with Richard

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.450
Pryor, cementing his status as a true screen
legend.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.829
In August 2016, when Wilder died at the age
of 83 from complications from Alzheimer's

00:01:23.829 --> 00:01:26.859
disease, his passing was quite unexpected.

00:01:26.859 --> 00:01:30.890
He'd apparently concealed his condition from
the public because the actor "simply couldn't

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.209
bear the idea of one less smile in the world."

00:01:34.209 --> 00:01:36.329
Anton Yelchin

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:40.750
This Russian-American actor was just beginning
to emerge as a major young talent, earning

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:45.619
critical praise for his work in Green Room
and the Star Trek franchise, among other films.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:50.880
But he tragically passed away at the age of
27 when his vehicle rolled down his driveway

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.109
and pinned him against a brick pillar in a
bizarre accident at his home.

00:01:55.109 --> 00:01:56.399
Peter Vaughan

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:01.520
This tireless character actor was probably
best known to American audiences as Maester

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.969
Aemon on Game of Thrones, but he was also
an accomplished star of film and TV for decades

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:08.240
before he joined the HBO fantasy series.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.070
His standout roles in British comedies and
cult classic films made him a star in his

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.860
homeland before he traveled anywhere near
The Wall.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.890
He was 93.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.520
Garry Shandling

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.860
One of the most prominent stand-up comedians
of the 1980s, and a pioneer of the observational

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.300
comedy style, Garry Shandling went on to co-create
and star in two of the most forward-thinking

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:32.280
TV comedies ever made: his self-titled sitcom
and his mockumentary style dramedy The Larry

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.360
Sanders Show.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.290
Shandling would go on to make a formidable
big screen career for himself too, but it's

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:41.470
his TV work which made him a pop culture icon
before his death at his home at the age of

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.280
66.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.640
Alan Thicke

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.570
Thanks to his memorable turn as the Seaver
family patriarch on TV's Growing Pains, Alan

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:53.700
Thicke was beloved as a parental figure for
many children of the '80s.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.260
Alan Thicke was 69 when he passed, reportedly
after playing a game of hockey with his youngest

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.560
son.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.850
Patty Duke

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:05.360
At the age of just 16, Patty Duke became the
youngest-ever Academy Award winner for her

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.220
role as Helen Keller in 1962's The Miracle
Worker, and a year later, she began her small

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.990
screen turn as "identical cousins" on the
self-titled Patty Duke Show.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:18.640
Her career in film, television, and stage
would be long-lived, and she passed on her

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.640
acting gene to her son, Sean Astin of Lord
of the Rings fame.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.800
Duke was also a vocal advocate for mental
illness awareness after being diagnosed with

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.120
bipolar disorder.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.130
She died of sepsis at the age of 69.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.770
Garry Marshall

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:35.160
While this Hollywood legend might be best
known for his work behind the lens, Garry

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:38.090
Marshall was also a memorable actor in his
time.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.000
His boisterous personality made its way to
the big screen in Hocus Pocus and A League

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.470
of Their Own, along with a number of television
series.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.680
Marshall died at the age of 81.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.680
Kenny Baker

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:53.080
For Star Wars fans, Kenny Baker's face wasn't
the most recognizable part of his presence

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:58.780
— he was the actor who brought life to R2-D2
in six of the Star Wars films and became an

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.190
icon of that franchise.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:04.660
Before visiting a galaxy far, far away, though,
he was known for his work as a circus clown

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.660
and comedian.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.120
He was 81 when he passed away after a long
illness.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.380
Jon Polito

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:14.090
If you've ever seen a Coen Brothers film,
chances are you've seen Jon Polito at his

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.090
best.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.440
The long-working character actor appeared
in some of the directors' most acclaimed projects.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:23.740
All told, Polito appeared in more than 100
movies and TV shows over the course of a three-decades-long

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.240
career and was 65 when he died of blood cancer.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.670
Alexis Arquette

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.580
Transgender actress Alexis Arquette was a
prominent member of her acting family and

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.500
was memorable for her big screen roles in
Pulp Fiction and The Wedding Singer as well

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.980
as her activism for LGBTQ issues.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.650
She was 47 when she passed away.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:43.810
Robert Vaughn

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:48.670
Legendary small screen star Robert Vaughn
thrived for decades in the action show sphere.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:52.140
He is perhaps best known for his work in The
Man from U.N.C.L.E. and The A-Team.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:56.450
Vaughn was also among the first actors ever
to speak out about political views, working

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:01.770
with several anti-Vietnam War organizations
during his prime, and received a Ph.D. in

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.770
communications.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:03.950
He was 83.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:05.150
Ron Glass

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:10.889
With not one but two cult hits on the small
screen, Ron Glass is best known for his scene-stealing

00:05:10.889 --> 00:05:15.350
work as Sergeant Harris in Barney Miller,
but sci-fi fans will probably know him best

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:19.730
for his role as Shepherd Book in the short-lived
and beloved series Firefly.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.810
He was 71.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.290
Alice Drummond

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:28.160
One of the most recognizable character actresses
of all time, Alice Drummond popped up in dozens

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.230
of movies and TV shows since the late '60s,
when she moved from the New York stage to

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.230
the screen.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:36.731
One of her most famous appearances may have
been in the original Ghostbusters, but she

00:05:36.731 --> 00:05:42.360
starred in dozens of films and TV shows before
passing away at the age of 88.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.900
Margaret Whitton

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:48.460
Major League fans might remember Margaret
Whitton best for her turn as the mean team

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:52.870
owner Rachel Phelps, but in real life she
was an avid fan of the sport.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:57.840
The actress worked on multiple media throughout
her career, including movies and the stage,

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.889
and was 67 when she died.

00:05:59.889 --> 00:06:01.620
Zsa Zsa Gabor

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:07.310
A predecessor of Paris Hilton and Kim Kardashian,
Zsa Zsa Gabor pioneered the idea of being

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:08.550
"famous for being famous."

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:13.310
The Hungarian-born Gabor was married at least
eight times, almost always to wealthy tycoons

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.740
of one sort or another.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:20.270
She still managed an acting career of sorts,
appearing in films and TV shows in the '50s

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.980
and '60s, such as the original Moulin Rouge,
and as the seductive Minerva on the campy

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:25.980
Batman.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:29.930
After suffering from a series of illnesses
and injuries over the past few years, Gabor

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.250
passed away at the age of 99 on December 18.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.610
Thanks for watching!

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.370
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.790
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

